1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,956
Robbie, this new Walkman is absolutely wonderful.

2
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
Richard and Marilyn bought it for me for my birthday.

3
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
They're so thoughtful.

4
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:16,350
You are very lucky, Robbie, to have such a nice family.

5
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,868
Is something wrong, Alexandra?

6
00:00:18,868 --> 00:00:20,846
No, nothing.

7
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:22,346
Yes, there is.

8
00:00:22,346 --> 00:00:24,464
I can tell.

9
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:26,802
What's the matter?

10
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:29,780
Come on, you can tell me.

11
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,780
What's up?

12
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:32,758
I don't know.

13
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:37,736
Something's wrong.

14
00:00:37,736 --> 00:00:41,692
OK, let's talk.

15
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:46,397
I received a letter from my parents this morning.

16
00:00:46,397 --> 00:00:49,447
Did they write some bad news?

17
00:00:49,447 --> 00:00:50,625
No.

18
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:53,603
Well, then why are you so sad?

19
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:54,668
I miss them.

20
00:00:54,668 --> 00:01:03,691
I miss them very much.

21
00:01:03,691 --> 00:01:04,383
I'm sorry, Alexandra.

22
00:01:04,383 --> 00:01:05,075
But I understand.

23
00:01:05,075 --> 00:01:07,415
The Molinas treat me so nicely,

24
00:01:07,415 --> 00:01:10,978
and I love being with your family so much ...

25
00:01:10,978 --> 00:01:13,614
but when I received the letter

26
00:01:13,614 --> 00:01:17,427
with photographs of my family, I cried.

27
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:20,405
I cried because I miss them all.

28
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:23,383
You really miss your family, don't you?

29
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:28,137
Yes. I know I must seem silly.

30
00:01:28,137 --> 00:01:30,979
It's not like I have nobody.

31
00:01:30,979 --> 00:01:33,210
I like the Molinas very much,

32
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:38,273
and they're so kind to me.

33
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:42,131
Hey, why don't we go out

34
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:43,891
for a cheeseburger and french fries?

35
00:01:43,891 --> 00:01:44,969
That'll cheer you up.

36
00:01:44,969 --> 00:01:47,207
And you can use my Walkman.

37
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,185
That's a good idea.

38
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,163
But if we go out,

39
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,724
please don't complain

40
00:01:56,724 --> 00:01:59,434
about your math teacher or your math homework.

41
00:01:59,434 --> 00:02:01,011
I want to have fun.

42
00:02:01,011 --> 00:02:02,096
So do I.

43
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:04,126
I have to turn off the lights,

44
00:02:04,126 --> 00:02:07,154
or else my father will get really angry.

45
00:02:07,154 --> 00:02:11,450
He says I never turn them out when I leave.

46
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:17,486
If they come home and they're on ...

47
00:02:17,486 --> 00:02:20,297
Do you hear something?

48
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:20,631
Yes.

49
00:02:20,631 --> 00:02:21,631
What was that?

50
00:02:21,631 --> 00:02:24,771
It sounded like a dog barking.

51
00:02:24,771 --> 00:02:32,834
It sounded like a dog barking right here.

52
00:02:32,834 --> 00:02:33,034
Yeah.

53
00:02:32,834 --> 00:02:35,140
A dog!

54
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:35,997
A springer spaniel!

55
00:02:35,997 --> 00:02:37,832
Come on in!

56
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:39,432
Make yourself at home.

57
00:02:39,432 --> 00:02:49,744
Oh, you poor little thing.

58
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,744
Come on.

59
00:02:51,744 --> 00:02:53,077
Poor baby.

60
00:02:53,077 --> 00:02:55,700
Where did you come from?

61
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,678
Her name's Gemma,

62
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:02,096
and she belongs to Mr. and Mrs. Levinson.

63
00:03:02,096 --> 00:03:03,856
There's a phone number --

64
00:03:03,856 --> 00:03:08,945
five five five ... eight four four eight.

65
00:03:08,945 --> 00:03:12,414
Robbie, maybe you should call them

66
00:03:12,414 --> 00:03:16,545
and tell the Levinsons we have their cute little spaniel.

67
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:18,265
I've always wanted a springer spaniel.

68
00:03:18,265 --> 00:03:36,913
She's so cute.

69
00:03:36,913 --> 00:03:42,994
The number you are calling -- 555-8448 --

70
00:03:42,994 --> 00:03:46,325
is no longer in service.

71
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:52,281
The number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,259
Oh, you poor, poor baby.

73
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:58,237
You've lost your family.

74
00:03:58,237 --> 00:03:59,137
We'll find them.

75
00:03:59,137 --> 00:04:02,137
Don't worry, Alexandra.
